"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with an initial budget approval of $2M, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, the testing phase, and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining an onboarding session on September 10th. Omar Jensen is leading the development phase, which follows the design phase. User interface enhancements are planned for October, and feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. A celebration for the testing phase milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
